{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And behold, YHWH stood over him.</b> We do not find thus with the rest of the patriarchs. Rabbi Simon said: The king does not stand over his field — neither when it is plowed nor when it is sown — but rather when the grain stands in the heap. Thus: Abraham plowed it, as it is said: ״קום התהלך בארץ״. Isaac sowed it, as it is said: ״ויזרע יצחק״. Jacob came — he is the heap of grain, as it is said: ״קדש ישראל לה׳ ראשית תבואתה״ — [therefore HaShem] stood over him." "<b>The land upon which you lie.</b> That is: that land upon which you lie — to you I give it, and on your own you will break through all the winds and conquer all around you, as is done for important horsemen, to whom they give a little ground and they conquer by their might all the surroundings."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:15.634815334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}